---
// How I work: from inside the clinic, one clinic at a time. Kept to what a
// clinic owner needs to know, not a method they could hand to someone else.
---
<section id="how" class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head rv">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> How I work</p>
      <h2>From inside the clinic, one clinic at a time.</h2>
      <p class="lead">I am not a vendor with a product to install. I spend time in the clinic, see where the day gets stuck, build the piece that fixes it, and stay around while it settles in.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="hw">
      <ol class="hw-steps rv">
        <li>
          <div>
            <h3>I start by spending time on your floor.</h3>
            <p>A few days at the front desk, in the testing rooms and in the exam lanes, noticing what people re-type, re-check, or walk down the hall to find out.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <h3>Then I build the piece that is missing.</h3>
            <p>One thing at a time, over weeks rather than months. Staff see it early and tell me what is wrong with it, and I keep adjusting until it feels natural to them.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <h3>It works alongside the EMR you already have.</h3>
            <p>Nothing is replaced and nobody learns a new system. Your patient information stays inside your clinic.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <h3>I stay involved.</h3>
            <p>Once something is running I keep an eye on it, and I am a message away when the clinic wants it to do something new.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <div class="hw-side rv">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Right now</h3>
          <div class="hw-status">
            <div class="row"><span>Working with</span><b>Tri-City Eye Care, Kitchener, Ontario</b></div>
            <div class="row"><span>Since</span><b>2026</b></div>
            <div class="row"><span>EMR</span><b>OSCAR. Others on request.</b></div>
            <div class="row"><span>Next opening</span><b>One clinic, 2027</b></div>
            <div class="row"><span>Best way in</span><b>An introduction, or a note below</b></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>A good fit</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>A busy clinic with several rooms and several roles.</li>
            <li>An owner or manager who feels like the glue holding the systems together.</li>
            <li>A team open to small changes that add up.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card quiet">
          <h3>Probably not a fit</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>A clinic looking to replace its EMR. I build alongside yours, not instead of it.</li>
            <li>A single-room office where the desk can already see everything.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
